%N A400934 a(1) = 1; for n > 1, a(n) is the smallest number > 1 such that it shares a factor with 0 to a(n)-1 previous terms.
%C A400934 The terms are nondecreasing, and each prime p appears in p consecutive terms. The missing numbers begin 6, 10, 12, 14, 18, 20, 22, 24, 26, 30, 33, 34, 35, ... .
%H A400934 Scott R. Shannon, <a href="/A400934/b400934.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A400934 a(7) = 4 as as 4 shares a factor with two previous terms, a(1) and a(2), and 0 <= 2 <= 4-1 = 3.
